[27.493, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mGit Diff Review: \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mdocs(mini-a): update documentation and MCP catalog\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[m\r\n\r\n\u001b[4mSummary of Changes\u001b[m\r\nThe commit updates documentation across five files (\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mcheatsheet.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mconfiguration.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mfeatures.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmcp-catalog.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mwhats-new.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m) to reflect new features including durable memory, Markdown persistence, cross-wiki graph traversal, and new\r\nAWS MCP servers (Athena and S3 Select).\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m1. Bugs & Functional Issues\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mNo critical bugs found.\u001b[m The changes are primarily documentation updates. \r\n- \u001b[1mConsistency Check:\u001b[m The new \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmemoryinject=relevant\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m default is consistently mentioned in \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mconfiguration.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mfeatures.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m,\r\nand \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mwhats-new.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m.\r\n- \u001b[1mCommand Accuracy:\u001b[m The example command in \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mfeatures.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m for \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmemorymd=true\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m co"]
[27.493, "o", "rrectly specifies both \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmemorych\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m and\r\n\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmemorysessionch\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, which is important for avoiding global store corruption during testing.\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m2. Security Issues\u001b[m\r\n- \u001b[1mCredential Handling:\u001b[m The \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmcp-aws-athena\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m documentation correctly notes that \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33maccessKey\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m/\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33msecret\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m can be omitted in favor of\r\nenvironment credentials or instance roles, following security best practices.\r\n- \u001b[1mRead/Write Permissions:\u001b[m The documentation explicitly mentions that \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mathena-stop-query-execution\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m and\r\n\u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mathena-delete-query-results\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m require \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mreadwrite=true\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m, maintaining the security model of the tool.\r\n- \u001b[1mMemory Protection:\u001b[m The \"two separate runs\" confirmation requirement for promoting session memory to global memory is a good\r\nguardrail against poisoning the durable store with untrusted or transient content.\r\n\r\n\u001b[4m3. Code Style & Documentation Quality\u001b"]
[27.493, "o", "[m\r\n- \u001b[1mFormatting:\u001b[m The use of tables in \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mconfiguration.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m and \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mcheatsheet.md\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m remains consistent. \r\n- \u001b[1mClarity:\u001b[m The explanation of \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mmemoryinject=relevant\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m is clear and distinguishes well between \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33msummary\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m and \u001b[2m`\u001b[m\u001b[33mfull\u001b[m\u001b[2m`\u001b[m modes.\r\n- \u001b[1mTypo/Grammar:\u001b[m No obvious typos detected in the added text. The terminology (e.g., \"durable records\", \"cross-wiki hints\") is\r\nconsistent with the rest of the documentation.\r\n\r\n\u001b[4mFinal Verdict\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mLGTM (Looks Good To Me).\u001b[m The documentation is comprehensive, follows the project's style, and accurately describes the new\r\ncapabilities without introducing security risks.\r\n"]
